When performing file reads or external inspections (such as PDF parsing), wrap the operations in try-catch blocks to catch errors and convert them into stable, typed failure diagnostics with a nonzero fail-closed exit code. This prevents raw file system errors from crashing the script when reading PDF files.

```javascript
      try {
